    "body": "What I am worried about is that we might accidentally break the different styling of the admin/non-admin username in the future and not notice, we are currently doing a lot of refactoring for the format string release and this is the sort of thing that could easily slip in. While not idea we already do have quite a few tests that depend on the environment in which the tests are being run, such as [test/testsuite/python](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/tests/testsuite/python.rs), so I don't see it as a major issue to add more tests that depends on the environment. So far we have used the `#[ignore]` macro to indicate if a test depends on the environment in which it is run. I don't think this is an ideal situation as there is still some gaps in the test coverage but it feels more complete to me (please correct me if I'm wrong). I guess the ideal situation would be to see if we can add some mocks for this so it doesn't depend on the environment but that would very probably involve a big refactor of the module.",
