    "body": "Well, apart from determining that the same code run twice has the same result, changing the code to test if we are in admin mode to set the \"expected\" result has little added value.\r\nWe could implement a flag in the context to determine if (or not) the user is an admin.\r\nlike an is_admin : Option<bool> that we could set before testing the module.\r\nThis has also its drawbacks. \r\nLet me know.\r\n",
